If you string enough of them together, you can build literally any computer processor

12:50.980 --> 12:51.660
in the world.

12:51.860 --> 12:52.820
It's the building block.

12:53.000 --> 12:58.120
But doing a NAND operation in this physical landscape requires some very specific choreography.

12:58.640 --> 13:02.700
You have to manipulate the shape of the bowls over time to map those four initial

13:02.700 --> 13:05.080
states to their correct final destinations.

13:05.480 --> 13:08.160
Let's actually map out that choreography because I think it helps.

13:08.160 --> 13:10.420
We start with our four bowls on the table.

13:10.900 --> 13:14.100
Zero, zero, zero, ten, zero, one, eleven.

13:14.100 --> 13:20.040
To complete a NAND gate's internal intermediate step, what the paper calls the erasure pair,

13:20.560 --> 13:21.900
what has to happen physically?

13:22.260 --> 13:28.140
Well, the truth table of a NAND gate dictates that two of these populations, the inputs

13:28.140 --> 13:31.100
zero, zero, and ten, must be forced together.

13:31.480 --> 13:33.900
They have to merge into a single well.

13:34.160 --> 13:34.380
Okay.

13:34.440 --> 13:36.700
Let's say we were merging them both into the ten bowl.

13:36.700 --> 13:44.240
Yes, but simultaneously, the other two populations, the inputs ura one and eleven, must not merge.

13:44.360 --> 13:45.340
They have to stay separated.

13:45.500 --> 13:49.320
They must remain distinct and apart from each other throughout the entire cycle.

13:49.480 --> 13:52.860
Okay, I want to flesh out an analogy here so we can really see the physical problem.

13:52.920 --> 13:53.420
Let's hear it.

13:53.420 --> 13:58.200
Imagine a massive concrete skate park with four deep bowls.

13:58.360 --> 13:59.000
Okay, four bowls.

13:59.320 --> 14:01.920
We have four skaters, one starting at the bottom of each bowl.

14:02.420 --> 14:07.720
To execute our logical operation, we have this giant earthquake machine that can warp and tilt

14:07.720 --> 14:09.320
the concrete of the entire park.

14:09.420 --> 14:10.940
The external magnetic field.

14:11.060 --> 14:11.520
Exactly.

14:12.060 --> 14:16.320
And by the end of our earthquake, the skater from bowl zero and the skater from bowl ten

